            {
                "entry_id": "5911f7c7-2697-3608-a41f-6392c0559f30",
                "word": "blanchisseuse",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "97487f85-9db4-49f2-bfbe-e86285e0a79c",
                        "entry_id": "5911f7c7-2697-3608-a41f-6392c0559f30",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "blanchisseuses"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "aaeddc79-4dd3-479e-bec5-8f4da5e7441f",
                        "entry_id": "5911f7c7-2697-3608-a41f-6392c0559f30",
                        "tags": [
                            "masculine"
                        ],
                        "form": "blanchisseur"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "12ab9600-a71e-3e7a-b3c0-3b58b1598ac1",
                        "entry_id": "5911f7c7-2697-3608-a41f-6392c0559f30",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Femme qui blanchit du linge, des toiles, de la cire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3e1b6fc-e384-4475-824a-7a5ef9a0d08a",
                                "sense_id": "12ab9600-a71e-3e7a-b3c0-3b58b1598ac1",
                                "text": "Il y avait grand vacarme de blanchisseuses ; elles criaient, parlaient, chantaient du matin au soir le long du bord."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "231186de-e06d-4586-866c-fd21c2f91c34",
                                "sense_id": "12ab9600-a71e-3e7a-b3c0-3b58b1598ac1",
                                "text": "Il s’agit de lâcher cette petite fille chez une blanchisseuse, la sœur à Godet, et qu’elle s’y impatronise…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cfa40c81-6f67-4ce7-a84f-2f2b0228d63e",
                                "sense_id": "12ab9600-a71e-3e7a-b3c0-3b58b1598ac1",
                                "text": "GUSTAVE – Qu’a-t-il depuis que nous sommes ici à fouiller dans ces vieux papiers ?\nJULIETTE – Je ne sais pas. Il est un peu fou. Mais comme il est en même temps méticuleux, cela donne des résultats extraordinaires. Il doit chercher une vieille note de blanchisseuse."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2a0f46b5-15f8-44f6-8539-ac44ebcfe82a",
                        "source_entry_id": "5911f7c7-2697-3608-a41f-6392c0559f30",
                        "source_sense_id": "12ab9600-a71e-3e7a-b3c0-3b58b1598ac1",
                        "target_lang_word": "bleacher",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bleacher",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99bf2872-ec40-354a-9abf-42641239abe0",
                                        "entry_id": "1e143656-bc00-35ea-ada6-be3219c3cd82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who, or that which, bleaches."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "791f2912-6b30-3ffe-9a12-72a532c6784f",
                                        "entry_id": "1e143656-bc00-35ea-ada6-be3219c3cd82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A stand of tiered planks used as seating for spectators, often outdoors."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "plural-normally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40b7b53b-8297-4b54-bb67-cbb4e6694afd",
                                                "sense_id": "791f2912-6b30-3ffe-9a12-72a532c6784f",
                                                "text": "There could be a rough crowd out in the bleachers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c736921-fb2d-41c7-9473-0717b4b65d59",
                                                "sense_id": "791f2912-6b30-3ffe-9a12-72a532c6784f",
                                                "text": "It seemed silly for the crowd to applaud or groan over what you had already felt in your fingers or even in your arms as you braced to shoot or for that matter in your eyes: when he was hot he could see the separate threads wound into the strings looping the hoop. Yet at the start of the game when you came out for warm-up and could see all the town clunkers sitting in the back of the bleachers elbowing each other and the cheerleaders wisecracking with the racier male teachers, the crowd then seemed right inside you, your liver and lungs and stomach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a219fe3-7a4d-4d4b-9bdc-7b44f0cb6846",
                                                "sense_id": "791f2912-6b30-3ffe-9a12-72a532c6784f",
                                                "text": "Warnings such as \"watch your step\" can be provided when there is a small step off a bleacher to the pavement or ground level."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc108684-8dbd-41ba-bc3e-c1771c2f1e63",
                                                "sense_id": "791f2912-6b30-3ffe-9a12-72a532c6784f",
                                                "text": "We prefer bleacher seats to Grandstand Sections 1-9. And in truth, quite a few bleacher seats offer a better view of the action than the Right Field Boxes do. Bleacher seats are made of comfortable plastic, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e9af4741-510e-3cf0-b934-340518a89b61",
                                        "entry_id": "1e143656-bc00-35ea-ada6-be3219c3cd82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The tiered seating provided for the audience at a television filming."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "broadly",
                                            "plural-normally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01653143-cfbd-42c8-b213-9e231256c081",
                                                "sense_id": "e9af4741-510e-3cf0-b934-340518a89b61",
                                                "text": "In practice, audience members often have badly obstructed views of the sets—whether due to obstructive camera dollies and production personnel or viewers sitting in the bleachers off to the side of the set that is currently being used."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bd26c2d1-64a1-40fd-b3d1-6ef9bcf8cd0c",
                        "source_entry_id": "5911f7c7-2697-3608-a41f-6392c0559f30",
                        "source_sense_id": "12ab9600-a71e-3e7a-b3c0-3b58b1598ac1",
                        "target_lang_word": "laundress",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "laundress",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37b1c869-5c6b-3041-8821-7804e594e76c",
                                        "entry_id": "299ce9a5-ebd0-3539-a982-1f4c5873e9c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of washerwoman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ef5a31c-0f6d-4d76-827d-c491adb342b7",
                                                "sense_id": "37b1c869-5c6b-3041-8821-7804e594e76c",
                                                "text": "I tell thee ſhameleſſe girle,\nThou ſhalt be Landreſſe to my waiting maide:"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "laundress",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c86b995d-1e0e-3646-acde-4bea65a7bbb0",
                                        "entry_id": "233b72bd-bd22-313a-8e1f-0384f099dfd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To act as a laundress."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1780522a-56e5-4dd4-b557-3ab9cf1daecb",
                                                "sense_id": "c86b995d-1e0e-3646-acde-4bea65a7bbb0",
                                                "text": "‘Sir,’ said Mrs. Crupp, in a tone approaching to severity, ‘I’ve laundressed other young gentlemen besides yourself. […]’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d4a82f4-8332-4631-9698-88069da0136a",
                                                "sense_id": "c86b995d-1e0e-3646-acde-4bea65a7bbb0",
                                                "text": "And oh, my dears, real washing is very different work from the dolls’ laundressing—standing round a wash-hand basin placed on a nursery chair, and wasting ever so much beautiful honey-soap in nice clean hot water […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "776ba401-1c6b-4b3d-be09-05955df3e7d2",
                                                "sense_id": "c86b995d-1e0e-3646-acde-4bea65a7bbb0",
                                                "text": "2007, Lawrence Hill, The Book of Negroes (Someone Knows My Name), New York: Norton, Book Three, p. 260,\nMama got herself free before she had me, and she was laundressing for the British since my early days."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cb32d21b-f220-432b-bae1-8bf333772cd6",
                        "source_entry_id": "5911f7c7-2697-3608-a41f-6392c0559f30",
                        "source_sense_id": "12ab9600-a71e-3e7a-b3c0-3b58b1598ac1",
                        "target_lang_word": "wasvrouw",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wasvrouw",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd22aeab-17c2-3828-a295-f7d384e1f099",
                                        "entry_id": "976aa651-184a-3e58-9ceb-4855ace62e57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "vrouw die voor haar beroep de was doet"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4887e625-d278-4c10-9ac4-ed1c7bd88fcb",
                                                "sense_id": "fd22aeab-17c2-3828-a295-f7d384e1f099",
                                                "text": "Heel de stad doet woensdag mee aan de festiviteiten. De straten in de binnenstad zijn bedekt met stro, terwijl de visnetten en de was in de straten worden gedroogd. De bevolking loopt in zestiende-eeuwse kledij, vissers leuren met ’versche visch’ en wasvrouwen doen aan de waterkant de was."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddf02d4b-b94d-47b1-825d-ecf3639d8d40",
                                                "sense_id": "fd22aeab-17c2-3828-a295-f7d384e1f099",
                                                "text": "De Wasvrouwen van Parijs was een economisch model. Vanuit de dure huizen kwam de was Die werd aangenomen door een vrouw, die gaf het door aan een ander en die gaf het weer door aan een ander totdat het uiteindelijk bij een echte wasvrouw aan de Seine terechtkwam."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b50e73e9-44bc-4222-9bb9-108f33167305",
                                                "sense_id": "fd22aeab-17c2-3828-a295-f7d384e1f099",
                                                "text": "`Mijn vader had van de rentmeester gehoord dat ze op de manor een wasmeisje zoeken.'`0 ja? En denk je dat de wasvrouw wat zal hebben aan zo'n kleintje als jij?'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "556aa938-bc73-4102-9740-1d7486268543",
                                                "sense_id": "fd22aeab-17c2-3828-a295-f7d384e1f099",
                                                "text": "In een hoek lag een hele berg linnengoed. De wasvrouw was nergens te bekennen."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
